iWave launches XMC/PrPMC module based on Freescale=92s MPC8640/ MPC8641

=93iWave announces industry first network engine with Quad Gigabit =
Ethernet ports=20
in XMC/PrPMC form factor, featuring Freescale=92s Power Architecture=AE =
technology=20
processors MPC8640/MPC8641(Single core) and MPC8640D(Dual core)=94

18thAugust 2010, Bangalore - India:iWave Systems Technologies, a leading =
embedded=20
design house Headquartered in Bangalore has recently released its =
iW-RainboW-G9,=20
a module based onFreescale=92s Power Architecture=AE technology processor =
MPC864x=20
with the XMC/PrPMC Industry standard form factor.=20

With the available 4x Serial RapidIO/ x8 PCI Express switched =
interconnects=20
along with Quad Gigabit Ethernet ports, this module provides high =
throughput=20
network engine solution with low latency=2E

This highly integrated, high performance module enables solution for =
Embedded=20
networking, Routers, switches and fast industrial control & automation, =
general=20
computing, embedded storage and time-critical applications.=20

This module, used as a standalone development platform, enables shortened =
development=20
time with cost savings which helps the customer to reduce overall project =
risk.=20


Commenting on this new module launch, Mr. Vivek Tyagi, Country Sales =
Manager,=20
Freescale Semiconductor India Pvt. Ltd., mentioned, =93iWave Systems =
Technologies,=20
an active Freescale Alliance partner, has come out with lot of solutions =
&=20
modules based on Freescale processors. Adding to this list, comes their =
latest=20
Power Architecture technology processor MPC864x based XMC/PrPMC module =
that=20
is suitable for developing high performance=A0networking, telecom, =
pervasive=20
computing applications.=94

When asked about the benefits of using this module, Mr.Kamaraj (Corporate =
Manager,=20
Product Engineering Group, iWave Systems Technologies) commented that =
=93This=20
module has Quad Gigabit Ethernet ports on front or rear panel of XMC =
module=20
along with the processor. It can be easily interfaced to other I/O, FPGA =
and=20
Carrier boards, either through the XMC or PrPMC interface. It also =
provides=20
the flexibility for the better System engineering, since it provides all =
the=20
4 GbE ports through the front panel interface as well as the expansion =
connector=20
interface=94=2E

MPC864x Processor Based XMC/PrPMC board features:

=D8=A0 Freescale MPC864x Processor @ 1GHz

=D8=A0 Power Architecture=99 e600 processor cores

=D8=A0 Quad Gigabit Ethernet Ports to front panel or rear panel connector =
of the=20
module=20

=D8=A0 4x Serial RapidIO / x8 PCI Express interface on XMC P15 Connector

=D8=A0 Dual 64-bit DDR Memory controller supported with optional ECC =
(Configurable=20
from 512MB to 2GB)=2E

=D8=A0 Up to 128MB NOR flash on Local bus controller

=D8=A0 Bootable 16KB I2C EEPROM

=D8=A0 UART Debug serial Port support

=D8=A0 5V and 3.3V Power input through PMC or XMC Interface

=D8=A0 5V Power input for Stand-Alone option

=D8=A0 Form factor - 149mm x 74mm standard single-width XMC size

=A0

System Block Diagram:

=A0

Availability:

This module is available now. Contact us for lead time information=2E

About=A0iWave Systems:

iWave Systems Technologies is an embedded Hardware and Software Turnkey =
Design=20
Services company, focused on providing integrated solutions for =
developing=20
innovative products and systems in the areas of Communication, =
Industrial,=20
Medical, Hand-held / HMI applications and Automotive preferably using the =
available=20
iWave developed CPU modules & FPGA IP Cores or with any new processor =
running=20
various OS (including WinCE, Linux, Android / QT, VxWorks). With its 10 =
year=20
expertise combined with its current 130 strong team, global presence and =
its=20
branch offices in Japan & Germany, iWave is poised to become an =
Independent=20
design house for the high tech Electronic Systems.=20

